However, a discrepancy arises when we observe certain PCIs indoors, but not outdoors, and vice versa. For instance, we observe one \tmo PCI outdoors but not indoors, and four PCIs indoors but not outdoors. This disparity is again attributed to the limitations of our measurement footprint. The indoor PCIs not observed outdoors were primarily captured on the north side of the building or on higher floors, while outdoor PCIs not observed indoors were captured on the south side of the parking lot.
