\vspace{7pt}
\noindent
7.2. \underline{Moving Phase:} As in the unmapping phase, the kernel takes multiple passes over the unmapped pages from the unmapping phase, and processes each page sequentially. It calls \verb|migrate_folio_move| to  move the page to its target destination. Once migration succeeds, all page locks both old and new are dropped. Finally, the new page is moved to the LRU list. 
