\section{Performance Evaluation}
\label{sec:exp}
Recall the use cases of page migration presented in \S~\ref{sec:use_case} in the context of an MMDB. 
In this section, we focus on the first 2 use cases and evaluate the performance of the two system calls \verb|move_pages| and \verb|move_pages2| in the context of an MMDB on 2 different hardware architectures, i.e., NUMA architecture (cf. \S~\ref{subsec:exp_numa}) and chiplet architecture (cf. \S~\ref{subsec:exp_chiplet}).
% \footnote{Since, CXL memory } 
We show that our proposed system call has significant performance improvements in both query throughput and page migration throughput. Additionally, we evaluate the impact of migration modes and batch size on the performance of \verb|move_pages2| (cf. \S~\ref{subsec:exp_sen}) ). 

