\begin{abstract}
Data trading is one of the key focuses of Web 3.0. However, all the current methods that rely on blockchain-based smart contracts for data exchange cannot support large-scale data trading while ensuring data security, which falls short of fulfilling the spirit of Web 3.0. 
% \yiming{This sounds like a very important claim. What are the reasons why current methods cannot support large-scale data trading? }
Even worse, there is currently a lack of discussion on the essential properties that large-scale data trading should satisfy. 
