The schedule operates as follows:
\begin{enumerate}
    \item First, we select only the outer two loops, shown with the black outline in the figure (line~\ref{line:matmul_schedule_par}), and we divide both of these loops into four chunks each (line~\ref{line:matmul_schedule_tile_par}). When the new dimensions are added above the old ones in the iteration space, we call it ``chunking.'' The resulting loop nest is shown in Figure~\ref{fig:juno_matmul_loops_chunk}.
