%\paragraph{Difference 2: Minimum degree estimation} When \(B\) is the normalized random walk Laplacian matrix, calculating \(B \cdot \mathbf{x}^{(t - 1)}\) does not require knowing the degrees of other nodes. This property simplifies computations within the edge LDP setting and is the main reason we select the normalized random walk Laplacian matrix over the normalized Laplacian matrix in our clustering algorithm. 

