Emotion understanding is a core challenge in affective computing, aiming to interpret human emotional states by integrating multimodal cues such as facial expressions, vocal tone, linguistic content, and visual contexts. While early efforts in {\itshape facial expression recognition} \cite{Attention-Driven-Xiaojiang, VGGFace2, EmoSet}, {\itshape audio emotion recognition} \cite{wav2vec2}, and {\itshape text sentiment analysis} \cite{InstructERC, EmoLLMs} laid the foundation for unimodal affect analysis, they often fall short in understanding the rich, context-dependent nature of emotions. %要 understanding才能衔接下文

Recent advances in Large Multimodal Models (LMMs) \cite{FromLLMtoLMM, Qwen-VL, Qwen2-VL, Qwen2.5-VL, MiniCPM-V, GPT-4} offer a new paradigm for emotion understanding. These models, originally developed for tasks such as visual question answering \cite{ScienceQA, TextVQA, VQAv2}, cross-modal reasoning \cite{MMBench, MME}, and image-text generation \cite{POPE, OCR-VQA}, possess strong generalization abilities across modalities but exhibit limitations in multimodal emotion-aware reasoning~\cite{GPT-4vwithemotion}. Motivated by this potential, recent work has explored adapting LMMs to multimodal emotion recognition (MER) tasks \cite{MER2023, MER2024, MERBench, DFEW, Emotion-LLaMA}, where models are fine-tuned to detect and explain emotions using combined signals from vision, audio, and text.

However, current methods remain constrained in several key ways. 
Most are limited to coarse-grained classification of basic emotions and lack the ability to generate interpretable or context-aware emotional reasoning. 
Moreover, fine-tuning LMMs for emotion-specific tasks often induces catastrophic forgetting \cite{More_Than_Catastrophic_Forgetting, Catastrophic_Forgetting_in_PEFT}, degrading the model's performance on general vision-language understanding. 
This trade-off between task specialization and generalization poses a major obstacle to building emotionally intelligent AI systems. 
The challenge is further exacerbated in complex real-world scenarios that require emotion inference across diverse contexts, nuanced reasoning, and temporal dynamics \cite{EMER, GPT-4vwithemotion, AffectGPT-old, AffectGPT-new}.

