 \subsection{Implementation Details}
\label{subsec:Implementation_Details}

Following the pre-training strategy described in Section~\ref{sec:Pre-training}, we utilized 3 NVIDIA A800 80GB GPUs for our training. We employed distributed training with DeepSpeed \cite{deepspeed} and enabled gradient checkpointing to optimize memory usage. To further reduce computational complexity, FlashAttention2 \cite{FlashAttention-2} was incorporated and the maximum image resolution was limited to $1280 \times 784$. 
We followed previous studies \cite{Qwen2-VL, MiniCPM-V} using Cross-Entropy (CE) loss as the optimization objective during training.
Due to hardware limitations and the rapid convergence of pre-trained model, the first two warm-up stages of pre-training were run for $1$ epoch, while the third stage was run for $3$ epochs.

Then, we proceeded to the instruction fine-tuning phase as detailed in Section~\ref{sec:Instruction Fine-tuning}. Multiple LoRA instances were applied to fine-tune the LLM backbone to reach more comprehensive emotion understanding.
Videos were limited to a maximum resolution of $448 \times 448$ and $3$ fps to balance coherence and memory consumption. Each LoRA instance was trained independently on different datasets for 5 epochs to prevent overfitting. Hyperparameter settings are summarize d in Table~\ref{tab:Hyperparameter}.



