\subsection{Ablation Study}
Regarding the ablation study, it is important to note that the original work of MFM achieved smoother results, albeit with a larger batch size (256). Due to hardware limitations, we were constrained to use a batch size of 128. Nevertheless, MFM represents the process of using flow matching training to determine the vector field; hence, it serves as our ablation study. In our case, we perform the training by directly determining the value without noise $x_1$. 
The results demonstrate the advantages of our direct training approach over the conventional flow-matching technique, even under similar training conditions.

