% \end{figure}

\section{Conclusion}
In this work, we proposed RF-3DGS+, an RRF framework tailored for THz communication scenarios where single-bounce scattering paths dominate. By incorporating full path length into the rendering process, RF-3DGS+ significantly improves reconstruction accuracy with minimal training data. The method addresses key limitations of previous 3D Gaussian-based models, especially the approximation of view depth. While currently limited to single-bounce paths, RF-3DGS+ is well-suited for short-range and indoor THz applications, and lays the groundwork for future extensions to multi-bounce scenarios and improved geometric representations.


