Recently, \citet{blauth2022improving} improved the approximation ratio to $\alpha+1-\varepsilon$ for the splittable case, and to $\alpha+2-2\varepsilon$ for the unsplittable case, 
and \citet{uncvrp} further improved the approximation ratio to $\alpha+1+\ln2-\varepsilon'$ for the unsplittable case using the LP rounding method, where $\varepsilon$ and $\varepsilon'$ are small positive constants related to $\alpha$. Notably, \citet{uncvrp} also gave a combinatorial $(\alpha+1.75-\varepsilon')$-approximation algorithm for the unsplittable case.
