%, a skill which only becomes more important as they progress further in their studies and careers as they begin to engage in collaboration, as well as developing the ability to read, understand and review code written by themselves and others.

This work presents AutoMCQ, a tool for the automatic generation of bespoke multiple-choice code comprehension questions by utilising a combination of automated unit testing and AI generated follow-up questions. %Each student receives a selection of simple questions based on a combination of their own code and the learning outcomes of the lesson. %, giving them an opportunity to evaluate their own progress in a way which does not embarrass them for their mistakes. 
%We provide a high level structure and code which allow integrating this process directly into the Moodle Virtual Learning Environment (VLE)~\footnote{https://moodle.org/} using the CodeRunner plugin~\footnote{https://coderunner.org.nz/}. 
This is not necessarily intended as a method of assigning or gating class credit, but rather as a tool for identifying cases where there might be a benefit to early intervention.

