let the finite-population game $\mathcal{G}_2$ with the same state-action space, dynamics, and rewards, but with population sizes $\tilde{N}_1$ and $\tilde{N}_2$ such that ${\tilde{N}_1}/{\tilde{N}_2} = {N_1}/{N_2}$ and $\min(\tilde{N}_1, \tilde{N}_2) \geq \min(N_1, N_2)$. 
%Let $\bfX^{\tilde{N}_1}_t$, $\bfY^{\tilde{N}_2}_t$, $\M^{\tilde{N}_1}_t$, and $\N^{\tilde{N}_2}_t$ denote the joint states and EDs for $\mathcal{G}_2$.
%
Then, the policies $\phi^*_t$ and $\psi^*_t$ remain ${\epsilon}$-optimal for the game $\mathcal{G}_2$.
\end{remark}
