\subsection{Constrained Rock-Paper-Scissors (cRPS)}\label{subsec:crps}

We now consider a non-trivial modification to the RPS problem by restricting the action space to $\mathcal{A} = \{\texttt{CW}, \texttt{Stay}\}$.
As shown in Figure~\ref{fig:rps-schematics},
with this restricted action space, the teams cannot immediately achieve their desired uniform distribution and need to strategically plan for the intermediate distributions before reaching the desired target uniform distribution.  
%
We again consider the fixed initial distributions  ${\mu}_{t=0} = [1, 0, 0]\t$ and ${\nu}_{t=0} = [0, 1, 0]\t$.
One may obtain analytically the conditions for the optimal trajectories of the cRPS game for these initial conditions.

