\textit{\textbf{Reverse:}} Interdisciplinary research requires caution as over-reliance on LLMs without domain expertise can lead to misinterpretation and reduced research rigor. Over-reliance on LLMs can also cause \textsc{AI hallucinations}—fabricated and inaccurate output—leading to misleading interpretations.% if results are blindly trusted.
Driven by probabilistic patterns, LLMs may generate plausible but incorrect conclusions, misattribute sources, or identify false patterns from noisy data, distorting findings and compromising research validity. One example is about using LLMs as annotators. While the model-to-model agreement can predict when LLMs could safely replace human annotators, it also highlights the potential for systemic bias where LLMs reinforce each other’s errors, creating a false perception of reliability~\cite{ahmed2024can}. Hence, while LLMs can support analysis and interpretation, human oversight is required. We need to keep in mind that LLMs currently cannot independently assess the validity of an argument, and critical thinking remains a human responsibility.
