\section{Algorithms for Second Price Matching and Second Price Perfect Matching}
In this section we present our main algorithm for the \textsc{Second Price Matching} problem and its special cases.
We show that our polynomial time algorithm solves \twopm and \twoppm to optimality for the degree constrained problem, when bidders bid on $2$ items each. In this setting, the input graph is assumed to have regular vertex degrees and by using this structure, we efficiently construct an optimal solution to the problem.

We also show that \ppm admits a formulation as a maximization problem over a monotone submodular function subject to a matroid constraint. Without leveraging any specific properties of \ppm, the maximum of the submodular function can be approximated by a factor $(1-1/e)$ by a canonical tight submodular maximization approximation algorithm \cite{calinescu2007maximizing}. 
