\label{subsection:model evaluation}
The \textit{final model score} is computed as: $C_{\text{total}} = \sum_{i=1}^{n} w_i C_i$, where $C_1$ (process model quality), $C_2$ (throughput time), and $C_3$ (implementation risk) contribute to the ranking (see Table~\ref{tab:config_comparison}). Although 532 leads in $C_1$ and $C_2$, 411 ranks best overall due to its balanced performance. This highlights the importance of multi-criteria evaluation integrating technical quality and practical feasibility. 

