After the new bounds have been set, a new random value between the bounds is picked, and the procedure repeats until $n_{\rm iterations}$ or if the value would be out of bound otherwise. 

The result of this search will be a schedule with the locally optimal values at every step. Afterward, the global utility is calculated of this schedule and compared with the previous utility (or $-\infty$ if the first schedule is generated and selected). The schedule can be chosen if the global utility has improved. 
