\subsection{Pair Comparison with Active Sampling}
% why PC
Considering the errors introduced by ACR for determining the cross-over point, we decided to use alternative test methodologies. Perez-Ortiz \textit{et al.}~\cite{perez2017practical} demonstrated that PC is more accurate method compared to ACR-HR. Similarly, Testolina \textit{et al.}~\cite{testolina2024fine} proposed using PC for fine-grained subjective visual quality assessment. We therefore considered PC to collect subjective data for resolution cross-over evaluation.

% why active sampling
% However, one of the biggest limitations of PC is its $O(n^2)$ time complexity~\cite{li2018hybrid}, where $n$ is the number of candidate stimuli to be tested. Several approaches have been proposed to reduce the number of pairs to be compared: \textit{(1)} Random sampling~\cite{xu2012hodgerank}, \textit{(2)} Sorting-based sampling~\cite{li2013boosting, ponomarenko2015image}, and \textit{(3)} Active sampling~\cite{li2018hybrid, mikhailiuk2021active}. Among these, Active Sampling has been shown to achieve the best performance~\cite{mohammadi2022evaluation}.
