%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%%
\section{Conclusion}
\label{Sec_Conclude}

We introduce SwitchMT, a novel methodology with adaptive task-switching strategy for multi-task RL that transitions between tasks based on the learning progress. 
By monitoring reward and internal dynamics of the model parameters, SwitchMT determines effective switching points, reducing training time and preventing overfitting. 
This dynamic adjustment enhances learning efficiency, simplifies the training process, and reduces the time and energy for hyperparameter tuning. 
Experimental results demonstrate that SwitchMT maintains competitive performance across multiple tasks compared to the state-of-the-art. 
These results highlight the potential of SwitchMT methodology to create resource-efficient agents capable of effectively learning multiple tasks.


